  "pages": [
    {
      "id": "how_built",
      "label": "How this app is built",
      "content": "# How this app is built\n\n**Three independent tables** — Guests, Vendors and Checklist — each with text, **select**, number and date fields.\n\n*Assigned To* on Checklist is a **User** field: it holds a workspace member.\n\nEvery table also has the **built-in fields** *Created by*, *Created at*, *Updated by* and *Updated at*.\n\n**Try it:** select Vendors and click **💬 + Add comments** to discuss each vendor.\n\n---\n\n## About this page: a report\n\nThis page is a **report**: markdown text plus live SQL. Open it in the schema editor under *Reports* and switch to *Edit* to see how it's written.\n\n**Markdown** gives you headings (`#`, `##`, `###`), **bold** (`**bold**`), *italic* (`*italic*`), `code` (backticks), bullet lists (lines starting `- `) and dividers (`---`).\n\n**SQL widgets** are blocks that start with three backticks and the word `report`, and end with three backticks. Each one runs its query every time the report opens and shows the result as a table. Queries are read-only.\n\n- Use **ids**, not labels: table ids (`guests`) and field ids (`rsvp`). RacerX finds this app's own copy of the table for you.\n- **Created at** / **Updated at** are seconds since 1970. Show them as dates with `date(created_at, 'unixepoch', 'localtime')`.\n- A **lookup** field stores the id of the record it points to. To show a name, join to that table (examples below).\n- Under each table, **+ SQL** shows the widget's query.\n- In any table's list view, **Copy SQL** copies the current sort and filters as a ready-made SQL widget to paste into a report.\n\n### RSVPs\n\n```report\nSELECT rsvp AS RSVP, COUNT(*) AS Guests\nFROM guests\nGROUP BY rsvp\nORDER BY Guests DESC\n```\n\n### Budget by vendor category\n\n```report\nSELECT category AS Category, COUNT(*) AS Vendors, SUM(price) AS \"Total ($)\"\nFROM vendors\nWHERE status <> 'Cancelled'\nGROUP BY category\nORDER BY \"Total ($)\" DESC\n```\n\n### Checklist progress\n\n**Done** is a checkbox, stored as 1 (ticked) or 0, so `SUM(done)` counts ticked tasks:\n\n```report\nSELECT SUM(done) AS Done, COUNT(*) - SUM(done) AS \"To do\", COUNT(*) AS Total\nFROM checklist\n```\n",
      "hidden": true
    }
  ],
